<article id="post-3617" class="post-3617 page type-page status-publish hentry no-post-thumbnail">
  <div class="entry-wrap">
            


<div class="entry-content content">


  <div id="cs-content" class="cs-content"><div id="x-section-1" class="x-section" style="margin: 0px;padding: 0px; background-color: transparent;" ><div id="" class="x-container" style="margin: 0px auto;padding: 20px 0 0; background-color:transparent;" ><div  class="x-column x-sm x-1-1" style="padding: 0px;" ><div class="x-row e3617-e4 m2sh-0 m2sh-1 m2sh-4 m2sh-5"><div class="x-row-inner"><div class="x-col e3617-e5 m2sh-8 m2sh-9"><a  class="x-img x-img-link x-img-none" style="margin:0 auto; display:block;" href="https://jcebmo.org/election-information/on-the-ballot/"  target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"   data-options="thumbnail: '14904:full'"><img decoding="async" src="https://jcebmo.org/wp-content/uploads/VoterLookup-Sep-22-2026-03_11_58-PM-e1790109611254.png" alt="On the Ballot"></a><div id="" class="x-text" style="padding-top: 2em;" ><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>EASTERN JACKSON COUNTY</strong> voters (all of Jackson County outside of the Kansas City city limits)  click the above image to look up your voter information.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Residents of <strong>JACKSON COUNTY</strong> who live in <strong>KANSAS CITY </strong>city limits will need to contact the <strong>KANSAS CITY ELECTION BOARD </strong>at <strong><span style="color: #bb0000;"><a href="https://www.kceb.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #bb0000;">https://www.kceb.org</a></span></strong></p>
</div></div><div class="x-col e3617-e8 m2sh-8 m2sh-9"><a  class="x-img x-img-link x-img-none"  href="https://jcebmo.org/wp-content/uploads/Absentee-Notice.png"  target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"   data-options="thumbnail: '14948:full'"><img decoding="async" src="https://jcebmo.org/wp-content/uploads/Absentee-Notice.png" alt="Voter Information Lookup"></a></div><div class="x-col e3617-e10 m2sh-8 m2sh-9"><a  class="x-img x-img-link x-img-none"  href="https://jcebmo.org/election-information/on-the-ballot/"  target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"   data-options="thumbnail: '14903:full'"><img decoding="async" src="https://jcebmo.org/wp-content/uploads/Next-Election-Sep-22-2026-03_10_35-PM-e1790109635825.png" alt="Voter Information Lookup"></a><a  class="x-img x-img-link x-img-none"  href="https://jcebmo.org/wp-content/uploads/notice-2.pdf"  target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"   data-options="thumbnail: '14896:full'"><img decoding="async" src="https://jcebmo.org/wp-content/uploads/Notice-Image-Sep-22-2026-03_07_08-PM-e1790107784531.png" alt="Voter Information Lookup"></a></div></div></div><div class="x-row e3617-e14 m2sh-0 m2sh-2 m2sh-3 m2sh-4 m2sh-6"><div class="x-row-inner"><div class="x-col e3617-e15 m2sh-8 m2sh-a"><div id="" class="x-text" style="" ><p class="h5" style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.5rem; text-align: left; ">PUBLIC NOTICE</p>
</div></div></div></div><div class="x-row e3617-e17 m2sh-0 m2sh-1 m2sh-3 m2sh-4 m2sh-7"><div class="x-row-inner"><div class="x-col e3617-e18 m2sh-8 m2sh-9"><div id="" class="x-text cs-ta-left" style="" ><p style="font-size: 1.25em; font-weight: bold; color: #333333;"><span style="color: #a80000;">Absentee Voting in Person:</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Excuse Absentee voting</span> for the November 3, 2026 General Election begins six weeks before Election Day. September 22-November 2</strong></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong><u>Independence Absentee Office</u></strong></span><br />
<span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>110 N. Liberty St.</strong></span><br />
<span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>Independence, MO 64050</strong></span></p>
<ul>
<li><span style="color: #a80000;">Office hours are Monday – Friday 8:30 am to 5:00 pm (we do not close for lunch).</span></li>
<li><span style="color: #a80000;">We will be open on two Saturday's, October 24, 2026 and October 31, 2026. The office hours are 8:30 am- 12:30 pm</span></li>
<li><span style="color: #a80000;"><span style="font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">For the first four weeks of absentee voting you must pick from one of the acceptable excuses.</span></span></li>
<li><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>Reasons you can vote absentee:<a href="https://jcebmo.org/voter-information/absentee-voting/" style="color: #a80000; text-decoration: underline;"><br />
CLICK HERE</a></strong></span></li>
</ul>
<p style="color: #a80000;"><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">No Excuse In-Person Absentee Voting</span> begins the second Tuesday prior to an Election. </strong></span></p>
<ul>
<li><span style="color: #a80000;">There will be two locations to vote absentee starting October 20, 2026.</span></li>
<li><span style="color: #a80000;">Open Monday through Friday from 8:30 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. We do not close for lunch.</span></li>
<li><span style="color: #a80000;">Both locations will be open on two Saturday's, October 24, 2026 and October 31, 2026. The office hours are 8:30 am- 12:30 pm.</span></li>
</ul>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong><u>Independence Absentee Office</u></strong></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>110 N. Liberty St.</strong></span><br />
<span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>Independence, MO 64050</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong><u>Woods Chapel Absentee Office</u></strong></span></p>
<p><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>500 NE Woods Chapel Rd.</strong></span><br />
<span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>Lee’s Summit, MO 64064</strong></span></p>
<p><strong><span style="color: #a80000;"><a href="https://jcebmo.org/voter-information/absentee-voting/" style="color: #a80000; text-decoration: underline;"><br />
</a></span><br />
</strong></p>
</div><div id="" class="x-text cs-ta-left" style="" ><p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.25em; font-weight: bold; color: #333333;">Residents of Kansas City go to<br />
<a href="https://www.kceb.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #a80000; text-decoration: underline;"><br />
https://www.kceb.org<br />
</a> for your voting information.</p>
<p><strong>For more information, contact:</strong><br />
<strong>JCEB Offices – 215 N. Liberty, Independence, MO 64050 | (816) 325-4600 | absentee@jcebmo.org</strong></p>
<p><strong> </strong></p>
</div></div><div class="x-col e3617-e21 m2sh-8 m2sh-9"><img decoding="async"  class="x-img x-img-none"  src="https://jcebmo.org/wp-content/uploads/Bard-Meeting-Notice-Sep-22-2026-03_13_01-PM-e1790109656533.png" alt="Board  Meeting Notice image"><div id="" class="x-text" style="" ><p><strong><span style="color: #000000;">         Board of Election Commissioners Meeting</span></strong></p>
<p><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>                      <span style="text-decoration: underline;">JCEB BOARD MEETING </span></strong></span></p>
<p><strong>When:</strong>       Tuesday, October 20, 2026                                             @ 2:00 PM</p>
<p><strong>Where:     </strong>JCEB OFFICE via ZOOM or in person                          215 N Liberty St.                                                              Independence, Mo. 64050</p>
<p>The Jackson County Board of Election Commissioners will conduct a Regular Board meeting on October 20, 2026.</p>
<p>     Other items include:</p>
<ul>
<li>610.021(1) Legal Actions</li>
<li>610.021(2) Real Estate</li>
<li>610.021(3) Employment</li>
</ul>
<p>The public may attend the meeting by contacting one of the Directors prior to the meeting to obtain the login information.</p>
</div></div><div class="x-col e3617-e24 m2sh-8 m2sh-9"><div id="" class="x-text cs-ta-left" style="" ><p><strong><span style="color: #a80000;">                            <span style="text-decoration: underline;">PUBLIC NOTICE</span></span></strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="color: #a80000;"><strong>                 </strong><strong><u>PUBLIC TEST (<em>Tabulation Equipment</em>)</u></strong></span></p>
<p><strong><span style="color: #a80000;">             </span></strong><strong><span style="color: #a80000;"> </span>                                </strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><strong>Election:  </strong>November 3, 2026 General Election</p>
<p><strong>When:</strong>      October 30, 2026 @ 9:00 AM</p>
<p><strong>Where:    </strong>JCEB Office                                                                     215 N Liberty St.                                                             Independence, MO 64050</p>
<p><strong>Why:      </strong>State Statute 115.233 RSMo</p>
</div></div></div></div></div></div><div id="" class="x-container" style="margin: 0px auto;padding: 40px 0 0px; background-color:transparent;" ><div  class="x-column x-sm x-1-1" style="padding: 0px;" ><img decoding="async"  class="x-img x-img-none" style="padding-top:20px; margin:0 auto; display: block;" src="https://jcebmo.org/wp-content/uploads/jceb-wants-you.jpg" alt="JCEB  want  you  to be  a poll worket  earn  extra - image"><div id="" class="x-text" style="margin-top:2em;" ><p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.55em; font-weight: bold; color: #0b2d5d; margin-bottom: 0.5em;">Now Recruiting Poll Workers for 2025</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://jcebmo.org/election-information/election-workers/" style="text-decoration: underline;">CLICK HERE</a> to learn more about Election Worker duties, or call our office at <strong><span style="color: #bb0000;">816-325-4600</span> </strong>to inquire.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">For more Information view the Election Judge Instructional Presentation on the <a href="https://jcebmo.org/election-information/election-worker-training/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration: underline;">Election Worker Training</a> page.</p>
</div></div></div></div></div>
  

</div>


  </div>
</article>        
      
    </div>
  </div>



  

  <footer class="x-colophon top">
